   "line": "Second, what doesn't help: swiping away all your apps. Back in 2017, a customer emailed Apple's software chief to ask whether he force quits apps, and whether doing it preserves battery life. His reply, published by Daring Fireball, was two words: no and no. iOS freezes apps you're not using. Killing them means the phone has to load them from scratch next time, which costs more power, not less.",
